---
---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
		<title>EmDash Learn demo</title>
		<style>
			:root { color-scheme: light; }
			body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 52rem; margin: 4rem auto; padding: 0 1.25rem; color: #172033; line-height: 1.6; }
			h1 { max-width: 15ch; font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 6vw, 4rem); line-height: 1.05; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
			.lede { max-width: 44rem; color: #4a5568; font-size: 1.15rem; }
			.actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.75rem; margin-top: 2rem; }
			.action { border-radius: 0.5rem; padding: 0.7rem 1rem; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 650; }
			.primary { background: #3047d8; color: white; }
			.secondary { border: 1px solid #ccd2e0; color: #24334f; }
			.note { margin-top: 3rem; border-left: 3px solid #8aa0ff; padding-left: 1rem; color: #59657a; }
		</style>
	</head>
	<body>
		<main>
			<p>EmDash Learn</p>
			<h1>Publish a course, not a learner database.</h1>
			<p class="lede">
				This demo shows the plugin's complete public surface: a published course
				catalog, ordered lessons, anonymous device progress, and Knowledge Checks
				with immediate feedback.
			</p>
			<div class="actions">
				<a class="action primary" href="/catalog">Browse the course catalog</a>
				<a class="action secondary" href="/_emdash/admin/plugins/lms-core">
					Open plugin admin
				</a>
			</div>
			<p class="note">
				No sign-in is required, and Learn does not create a server account. Lesson
				completions and self-check results stay in this browser unless a verified
				EmDash account explicitly imports supported device progress.
			</p>
		</main>
	</body>
</html>
